---
import { YouTube } from '@astro-community/astro-embed-youtube';
import Layout from '~/layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import Lightbox from '~/components/feed/Lightbox.astro';

const metadata = {
  title: 'Launch My Dog',
  description:
    'The hot-dog flinging physics-based puzzle game where you launch a hot dog into a bun. Things get in the way. Collect toppings, avoid Ketchup, experience anti-gravity, and go through portals to get your hot dog into its hot dog bun.',
};

const facts = [
  { label: 'Platforms', value: 'iOS & Android' },
  { label: 'Released', value: 'July 10, 2021' },
  { label: 'Built with', value: 'Unity' },
];

const screenshots = [
  { src: '/images/launch-my-dog/screen-1.jpg', alt: 'Launch My Dog in-game' },
  { src: '/images/launch-my-dog/screen-2.jpg', alt: 'Launch My Dog main menu' },
  { src: '/images/launch-my-dog/screen-3.jpg', alt: 'Launch My Dog in-game level 19' },
  { src: '/images/launch-my-dog/screen-4.jpg', alt: 'Launch My Dog in-game level 30' },
];

const h2Class = 'text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold font-heading tracking-tight dark:text-white mb-6';
---

<Layout metadata={metadata}>
  <!-- Hero -->
  <section
    class="relative bg-cover bg-center"
    style="background-image: url('/images/launch-my-dog/splash-bg.jpg');"
  >
    <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-black/60"></div>
    <div class="relative px-4 md:px-6 py-20 sm:py-28 mx-auto max-w-3xl text-left text-white">
      <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-6xl font-bold font-heading tracking-tighter mb-6">Launch My Dog</h1>
      <p class="text-lg md:text-xl mb-8">
        The hot-dog flinging physics-based puzzle game where you launch a hot dog into a bun. Things get in the way.
        Collect toppings, avoid ketchup, experience anti-gravity, and go through portals to get your hot dog into its
        hot dog bun.
      </p>
      <a
        href="#download"
        class="inline-block px-6 py-3 rounded-lg bg-white text-gray-900 font-semibold hover:bg-gray-200 transition"
      >
        Download
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

<!-- Trailer -->
  <section class="px-4 md:px-6 py-12 sm:py-16 mx-auto max-w-3xl">
    <div class="not-prose my-8 [&_lite-youtube]:!w-full [&_lite-youtube]:!max-w-none">
      <YouTube id="Z0nJEmJ8Ms8" />
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- About -->
  <section class="px-4 md:px-6 pb-12 sm:pb-16 mx-auto max-w-3xl">
    <h2 class={h2Class}>About the Game</h2>

    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-4 mb-10">
      {
        facts.map((fact) => (
          <div class="rounded-lg border border-gray-700 bg-gray-900 p-4 text-center">
            <p class="text-sm text-gray-400">{fact.label}</p>
            <p class="text-lg font-semibold text-white">{fact.value}</p>
          </div>
        ))
      }
    </div>

    <div class="prose lg:prose-xl dark:prose-invert max-w-none">
      <p>
        Launch My Dog is a tight, small game built for mobile, with trajectory prediction that adapts to whatever the hot dog is flying through, including gravity zones and portals.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
  
  <!-- Download -->
  <section class="px-4 md:px-6 pb-16 sm:pb-20 mx-auto max-w-3xl">
    <div id="download" class="text-center scroll-mt-24">
      <h2 class={h2Class}>Download</h2>
      <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-center gap-4">
        <a
          href="https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=com.NerdHerdNetwork.LaunchMyDog"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
        >
          <img src="/images/google-play-badge.png" alt="Get it on Google Play" class="h-14 w-auto" />
        </a>
        <a
          href="https://apps.apple.com/us/app/launch-my-dog/id1575435217"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
        >
          <img src="/images/app_store.svg" alt="Download on the App Store" class="h-14 w-auto" />
        </a>
      </div>
      <p class="mt-6 text-sm text-gray-500 dark:text-slate-400">
        Leaving a review is greatly appreciated. It boosts the game in search.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Screenshot gallery -->
  <section class="px-4 md:px-6 pb-12 sm:pb-16 mx-auto max-w-4xl">
    <h2 class={h2Class}>Screenshot Gallery</h2>
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
      {
        screenshots.map((shot) => (
          <figure>
            <button
              type="button"
              data-gallery="lmd-screenshots"
              data-full={shot.src}
              data-alt={shot.alt}
              aria-label={`View screenshot: ${shot.alt}`}
              class="block w-full overflow-hidden rounded-lg shadow-lg cursor-zoom-in"
            >
              <img
                src={shot.src}
                alt={shot.alt}
                loading="lazy"
                class="w-full h-auto hover:opacity-90 transition"
              />
            </button>
            <figcaption class="mt-2 text-sm text-center text-gray-500 dark:text-slate-400">{shot.alt}</figcaption>
          </figure>
        ))
      }
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Development story -->
  <section class="px-4 md:px-6 pb-12 sm:pb-16 mx-auto max-w-3xl">
    <h2 class={h2Class}>Development/Updates</h2>

    <ol class="border-l-2 border-gray-300 dark:border-gray-700 ml-1.5 space-y-10">
      <li class="relative pl-6">
        <span class="absolute -left-[7px] top-2 h-3 w-3 rounded-full bg-primary"></span>
        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold">Late 2016</h3>
        <p class="mt-1 text-muted dark:text-slate-400">
          A few months after Poke My Balls released, I had the idea in the middle of the night: launch a hot dog into a hot dog bun. I started working the very next morning.
          Over the next year, on and off, I built 108 levels across 12 mechanics. By summer 2018 it was
          technically complete, but there was no spark. It wasn't fun to play. It was also a bloated mess where I put band-aids over band-aid solutions. After a small power outage corrupted some of the files I left it behind.
        </p>
      </li>

      <li class="relative pl-6">
        <span class="absolute -left-[7px] top-2 h-3 w-3 rounded-full bg-primary"></span>
        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold">February 2020: starting over</h3>
        <p class="mt-1 text-muted dark:text-slate-400">
          Fresh off a Poke My Balls overhaul, I restarted from scratch. This time I wanted to fix problems at the
          root instead of piling workarounds on top of each other, I also began the search for the game's spark again. I looked at the launching itself, making it more fluid and human, rather than just a bunch of pre-set angles to choose from. It was much closer to Angry Birds.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-4">
          <YouTube id="rx-Eqx3rSQ0" />
        </div>
      </li>

      <li class="relative pl-6">
        <span class="absolute -left-[7px] top-2 h-3 w-3 rounded-full bg-primary"></span>
        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold">Planning and cutting scope</h3>
        <p class="mt-1 text-muted dark:text-slate-400">
          Late 2020, scope creep was getting the best of me. I had planned other modes, a cosmetic store, and even a level editor. Realizing this was too much, I wrote a planning document with a clear end goal and a due date of July 10th, 2021. Since university, a pandemic, and other projects ate more time than I expected, the scope shrank. The level editor, random levels and circuits were cut, and
          the level count dropped from 100 to 50 so every level could be unique and I could actually finish on time.
        </p>
      </li>

      <li class="relative pl-6">
        <span class="absolute -left-[7px] top-2 h-3 w-3 rounded-full bg-primary"></span>
        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold">The programming</h3>
        <p class="mt-1 text-muted dark:text-slate-400">
          With a smaller scope I could focus on what was already in the game. The physics are based on my high school
          AP physics equation sheets. Trajectory prediction adapts to different mediums and portals, so that you can accurtately predict the launch of the dog through whatever I've decided to throw at you.
          Portals are my favorite mechanic: they're physically accurate, and I used what I learned in
          linear algebra to build a shader that slices the hot dog's geometry at one portal and clones it out of the
          other.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-4">
          <YouTube id="TJ6HugnHiuw" />
        </div>
      </li>

      <li class="relative pl-6">
        <span class="absolute -left-[7px] top-2 h-3 w-3 rounded-full bg-primary"></span>
        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold">Optimizing and shipping</h3>
        <p class="mt-1 text-muted dark:text-slate-400">
          Since this was a mobile game with expensive physics, optimization mattered. The 2018 version loaded every
          level at once and only showed them when needed. This time I built a base scene with the UI and main menu and
          loaded levels additively, which let me push the physics harder and make levels more complex. After a few
          weeks of crunch and three nervous days waiting for Google Play's initial review, Launch My Dog released on July 10th, 2021, and the deadline was met.
        </p>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <Lightbox />
</Layout>